## What a real audit reveals

We recently reviewed a Lagos e-commerce store. The owner thought the site was performing well. The audit found:
- **Poor mobile navigation** — 62% of visitors could not reach checkout
- **Missing trust signals** — no reviews, no return policy, no phone number visible
- **Slow page speed** — product images were unoptimized
- **Weak CTAs** — the "Buy Now" button looked like a link

After fixing those four issues, their conversion rate doubled in three weeks.

That is the power of looking at your website like a **revenue tool**, not a digital brochure.

## Three things to fix before you spend more on marketing

If you cannot afford a full audit today, start here:

### 1. Make your phone number visible on every page
Put it in the header. Make it tappable on mobile. If a visitor has to search for how to call you, you have already lost them.

### 2. Shorten your forms
Every extra field kills conversions. Name, email, and one qualifying question is enough for a first touchpoint.

### 3. Speed up your mobile load time
Compress your images. Remove unused scripts. Nigerians browse mostly on mobile, and slow sites get abandoned fast.

